.TH SISTA-VERSION 3 "2026-10-09" "Sista"
.SH NAME
sista-version \- query the Sista header version
.SH LIBRARY
Header-only interface (no additional library required)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sista/version.hpp>

.B "#define SISTA_VERSION ..."
.B "#define SISTA_VERSION_MAJOR ..."
.B "#define SISTA_VERSION_MINOR ..."
.B "#define SISTA_VERSION_PATCH ..."
.B "const char *sista::getVersion();"
.B "int sista::getVersionMajor();"
.B "int sista::getVersionMinor();"
.B "int sista::getVersionPatch();"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The macros expose the version encoded by the installed headers.
The inline C++ functions return the same values in expression-friendly
form.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.B getVersion()
returns a static string in
.I MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH
form.
The component functions return the corresponding integer.
.SH CAVEATS
These are header values.
They do not independently inspect a dynamically loaded library, so
applications must not use them as a runtime ABI compatibility test.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sista-c-api (3),
.BR sista (7)
